  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">DELETE `SaveRequest.ContainerId`. Do not merely ignore it server-side — a field that still deserializes is a field a future change will start honouring again. Follow the `FolderPath` precedent at `SaveRequest.cs:29-34`: remove it and leave the reasoning at the deletion site.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner-Q1">The no-record branch derives the container from the **acting user's business unit**, server-side. Never from the request.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner-Q5">Returning the chosen container/drive id in the RESPONSE is required — the client needs `driveId`. Only ACCEPTING one is forbidden.</constraint>
    <constraint source="task-076">Reuse the record→container derivation task 076 already routes through. Do NOT add a second one. Exactly one container-selection model.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-003">If neither a record nor an acting-user business unit resolves, DENY. Never fall back to a config default in the record-bearing case.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-008">Authorization stays in endpoint filters. Do not move the decision into handler code.</constraint>
    <constraint source="build-plan">Do not solve any part of this by granting an SPE container permission. `GrantMembershipAsync` stays at zero callers.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The ProcessingJob payload (`OfficeService.cs:169`) must carry the SERVER-DERIVED container, not a client value. A persisted client value outlives the request and defeats the fix.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Do not widen `EntityAccessFilter.EntitySetByType` in this task — that is the Q4 change and the map is shared. Coordinate; re-verify this surface after it lands.</constraint>
  </constraints>

