  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Re-verify the shape at current HEAD before changing anything — line numbers in this POML were accurate 2026-08-30 but the folder-removal and sanitize commits have moved this file twice already. Confirm `ContainerId` still flows request → `OfficeService` → `OfficeStorageUploader`, and still lands in the job payload.</step>
    <step order="1">Inventory every producer and consumer of `SaveRequest.ContainerId` — server AND `src/client/office-addins/**`. Grep evidence required. A shipped add-in that sends it turns this from a deletion into a coordinated client change.</step>
    <step order="2">Server-derive the container: from the authorized record when `TargetEntity` is present (task 076's path); from the acting user's business unit when it is not. Thread the derived value into the job payload.</step>
    <step order="3">Delete `SaveRequest.ContainerId` and the `_emailProcessingOptions.DefaultContainerId` fallback in the record-bearing branch. Decide explicitly — and state in the notes — whether the config default survives for the no-record branch or is replaced by the BU derivation.</step>
    <step order="4">Tests: a request naming a container the caller may not reach is refused (or the field no longer exists — assert the contract, not just the behaviour); a save with no `TargetEntity` still lands in the acting user's BU container and nowhere else; the response still carries `driveId`.</step>
    <step order="5">Update `SpeWriteSinkContainerProvenanceGuardTests` — reclassify the Office sinks `ClientSupplied` → `ServerDerivedRecord`/`ServerDerivedConfig` and correct rows in `notes/task-083-sink-inventory.md`. The guard failing is the signal the change landed.</step>
    <step order="6">Build, tests, publish size vs the 44.96 MB baseline (ceiling 60), CVE scan. Placement Justification per CLAUDE.md §10.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If a shipped Office add-in build DOES send `ContainerId`, STOP. Deleting the field then breaks a deployed client and the fix gets reverted — which reopens the hole. Surface the coordinated-change decision instead of guessing.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the acting user's business unit does not resolve to exactly one container, STOP and surface it. Do not pick one, and do not fall back to the config default for a record-bearing save.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>Task 076 already derives a container from an authorized record; `EntityAccessFilter` already authorizes the target entity.</existing>
    <extension>Removes a client-supplied field and routes an existing write through the existing derivation. No new component, no new map, no new filter.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Any authenticated caller who writes the request JSON by hand chooses which SPE container receives the bytes, on an app-only MI write with no ACL backstop — and, because `TargetEntity` is optional and `EntityAccessFilter` passes through when it is absent, can do so without naming a record at all. In SPE, content placed in a shared container is permanently exposed to that container's members; there is no repair after the fact.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

